# GMP source

The cvc5 library in this package uses the GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic
Library (GMP), version @TAU_GMP_VERSION@. Where GMP is not a system package,
this package holds it as a separate shared library beside cvc5.

GMP is free software under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3
(LGPLv3), or the GNU General Public License, version 2. The license texts are
in this folder. Tau and cvc5 load GMP as a shared library, so you can replace
it with a build of your own.

The source of GMP is in the same GitHub release as this package:

- `gmp-@TAU_GMP_VERSION@.tar.bz2` is the GMP source release, unmodified
  (SHA-256 `@TAU_GMP_SHA256@`). The Linux and macOS packages build it as it is.
- `gmp-vcpkg-port-@TAU_GMP_VCPKG_SHORT@.tar.gz` is the vcpkg port that builds the
  GMP of the Windows packages: its portfile and the patches it applies to that
  release.
- `gmp-build-scripts-@TAU_GMP_VERSION@.tar.gz` holds the scripts that build GMP
  and cvc5.

The GMP source release is also at @TAU_GMP_URL@ and at
https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/gmp-@TAU_GMP_VERSION@.tar.bz2. The vcpkg port
is the `ports/gmp` folder of @TAU_GMP_VCPKG_REPO@ at commit
@TAU_GMP_VCPKG_COMMIT@. The GMP home page is https://gmplib.org/.
